{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01J4Z1vDWBMv8iNW8vth2i4i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013LuRzkfstXvVvRCsvocWwd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus areas are **methods** and **experiments**. Perform a blind review — do not speculate about author identity or paper quality tier.\n\n## Venue: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR)\nScoring: Overall Assessment 1-5 (half-point scale). Dimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5).\nAcceptance rate: ~21% for Main conference. Score 4 = acceptable for conference, 3 = Findings.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"How Stable Are LLM Benchmarks? Psychometric DIF Analysis of 5,227 Models Reveals 31% Temporal Item Instability\"\n\nThe paper applies Mantel-Haenszel Differential Item Functioning (MH-DIF) analysis from psychometrics to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items). Key findings:\n- 31.3% of MMLU items are ETS C-class (large DIF) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts\n- Random-split control: 0.18% (174× enrichment); permutation null: 0.21±0.09%, observed >345σ above\n- Cross-benchmark validation on 6 benchmarks: C% ranges 17.9-31.3%, all ≥45× enrichment, all random controls &lt;1%\n- Simpson's paradox: domain-level accuracy improvement positively predicts DIF (OR=1.55), but reverses after controlling for item difficulty/discrimination (OR=0.73). McFadden R²=0.0423, meaning 96% of DIF is item-specific.\n- Semi-synthetic validation: ΔTPR monotonically increases from +0.222 (p=0.3) to +0.674 (p=1.0). Cross-subject matching yields ΔFPR=0.000 vs within-subject FPR inflation of +0.186.\n- Ground truth meta-critique: DIF enrichment against Li et al. web-overlap labels is 0.96 (Jaccard=0.206), meaning web-overlap and DIF are orthogonal signals.\n- Despite 31% instability, ranking correlation remains ρ≈0.997 after removing all flagged items — massive measurement redundancy.\n- Proposes DIF audit protocol for benchmark maintainers.\n\n4 contributions claimed:\n1. Empirical discovery at scale (31.3% temporal DIF, 6 benchmarks, item-specific)\n2. Ground truth meta-critique (web-overlap orthogonal to DIF)\n3. Semi-synthetic validation framework (ΔTPR + cross-subject matching)\n4. DIF audit protocol\n\n## Experiment Design Reference\nThe full experiment plan includes these experiments. The paper covers some but not all:\n\n**Covered in paper:**\n- plan_001: MMLU temporal DIF (Table 1) — core result\n- plan_028: 6-benchmark cross-validation (Table 2) — MMLU, WinoGrande, TruthfulQA, ARC-Challenge, GSM8K, HellaSwag\n- plan_030: Simpson's paradox logistic regression (Table 3) — 4-model comparison\n- plan_011: Semi-synthetic contamination validation (Table 4) — dose-response with cross-subject matching\n- plan_029: Permutation null (text mention, 1000 iterations)\n- plan_010: Architecture stratification (text mention, 99.98% decoder-only)\n- plan_008: Graceful degradation (§4.6, replacement analysis up to 50%)\n- plan_009: Item-Focused Trees (§4.6, 81% concordance with MH)\n- plan_004: GSM8K portability of semi-synthetic framework (§4.5)\n\n**In Limitations/Discussion:**\n- plan_002: RL robustness — only 13 reasoning-RL models, mentioned as limitation\n- plan_005: Bifactor IRT equating — killed due to CFI=0.72, mentioned in limitations\n- plan_007: Cumulative Bayesian DIF — simulation, may be appendix-only\n\n**Correctly dropped:**\n- plan_003a/b/c: ConStat/DVD/ensemble — incompatible with \"characterization\" framing\n- plan_006: Item generation calibration — dependency killed\n\n## Your Task\nEvaluate the paper on these R1-specific dimensions:\n\n### 1. Methodological Soundness\n- Is MH-DIF correctly applied? Check: matching variable choice (cross-subject total score), ETS classification thresholds, BH-FDR correction, stratification.\n- Is the temporal binary split (2023 vs 2024-H1) well-justified? Does the permutation null adequately validate it?\n- Is the Simpson's paradox analysis methodologically sound? Check logistic regression specification, OR interpretation, LR test.\n- Is the semi-synthetic framework valid? Does the injection mechanism (flipping incorrect→correct) reasonably approximate differential contamination? Is ΔTPR the right metric?\n- Is the cross-subject matching innovation real? Does ΔFPR=0.000 hold under all conditions?\n\n### 2. Experimental Completeness\n- Are the experiments sufficient to support the 4 claims?\n- What's missing that a reviewer would ask for?\n- Are control conditions adequate (random split, permutation, BH-FDR)?\n\n### 3. Statistical Rigor\n- Multiple testing: Is BH-FDR at q=0.05 sufficient? Only 3/3918 items removed — is this surprising or expected?\n- Effect sizes: Are they reported alongside p-values?\n- Confidence intervals: Where are they missing?\n- The 98% IRT person misfit (|Lz|>2) — does this undermine MH-DIF results?\n\n### 4. Reproducibility\n- Is METABENCH public? Can experiments be reproduced?\n- Are hyperparameters (K strata, thresholds) specified?\n- Is code/data availability mentioned?\n\n### 5. Weaknesses\nList concrete weaknesses, ranked by severity. For each, state whether it's fixable in revision.\n\n### 6. Scores\nProvide:\n- Soundness (1-5)\n- Excitement (1-5)  \n- Reproducibility (1-5)\n- Overall Assessment (1-5, half-point scale)\n- Confidence (1-5)\n\nFormat your review as a structured report with clear section headers.","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25658,"cache_read_input_tokens":24182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25658},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08c58412-17e2-4f74-8